{
	"_comment": "Hotstring reader header and logical-value vectors, replayed by _shared/lua/test/toml_hotstring_reader_vectors_contract.lua on macOS and Linux. entry point: the hotstring TOML reader's parse_text(text) -> document, committed. text is the whole file. expect.committed is whether the source receipt is issued; a refused source exposes no section and no source entry (source_entries is then 0). On a committed text, sections lists, for each named section (a literal hotstring group name, not a key path), the output of its first entry; first_section is the first section in file order; source_entries is the number of source entries; meta_delays lists [_meta.sections.<name>] delays. A section header such as [[name]] names the literal group; [x.y] tables under [_meta] are metadata paths. Converted from toml_quoted_headers_contract.lua.",
	"entry_point": "hotstring TOML reader parse_text(text) -> document (sections, sections_order, source_entries, meta), committed",
	"drivers": {
		"macos": "Replays every vector.",
		"linux": "Replays every vector.",
		"windows": "Not ported: one AHK consumer must call the Windows hotstring TOML reader on each text and compare the committed verdict, the sections, their first output and order, the source entry count and the metadata delays."
	},
